  "reason": "The bug report shows that TIMESTAMP literals are not being grouped with their string literals (e.g., `TIMESTAMP '2020-01-01 00:00:00'` is split into two tokens instead of one). The root cause is that TIMESTAMP was classified as tokens.Keyword instead of tokens.Name.Builtin. By changing TIMESTAMP to tokens.Name.Builtin in sqlparse/keywords.py, it now matches the M_OPEN pattern in TypedLiteral class, allowing the group_typed_literal() function in grouping.py to properly group TIMESTAMP with its following string literal, just like DATE and INTERVAL already work. This directly addresses the reported issue."
}
